<style>
  .article-collection-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    column-gap: 16px;
    row-gap: 20px;
    padding: 20px 40px 40px 40px;
  }
  
  .graphics-article-title {
    display: block;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 20px;
    padding: 43px 20px 0 20px;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 440px;
    line-height: 26px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    opacity: 1;
    -moz-transition: all .3s ease-in-out;
    -webkit-transition: all .3s ease-in-out;
    -o-transition: all .3s ease-in-out;
    -ms-transition: all .3s ease-in-out;
    transition: all .3s ease-in-out;
  }
  
  
  .blog-img-caption {
    top: 10px;
  }
  
  .gallery {
    min-height: 10px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .graphics-article-title {
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 26px;
      top: 67px;
    }  
    .article-collection-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
      column-gap: 16px;
      row-gap: 20px;
      padding: 20px;
    }
  }
</style>

<div class="graphics-article-title" >
 {{ article.title }}
</div>
<div class="centered-article-text">
  <p>
    Greenpoint, Brooklyn has been the home of Adsum’s office, and a couple of the team members, for the last 4 years. It’s a special little nook of the city that, because of it’s awkward location, has remained relatively quiet and maintained a neighborhood feel. Unlike most of the city, it’s hard to just end up there. You have to want to be there, to be there. It’s the type of place that taking a walk to grab coffee or taking care of chores can still be a relaxed affair.
  	<br><br>
    We did just that on a recent warm afternoon, taking our offering of shorts and newly released and restocked socks & totes around the neighborhood.  
  </p>
</div>

